	(text "Temp Sensor\nSensor connector from the work space (orange 4-pin on old PL2). B1 -> MAX31865 (Pt100, 2-wire as fitted;\nlead resistance trimmed by a calibration offset in firmware). B3 passed to Specimen_Protection (Signal_list V2)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "80b6be23-870e-4c38-88bc-fa938d2e8c25")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- Pt100 front end for B1 (control sensor): MAX31865, 2-wire as fitted. Solder jumpers for 3/4-wire in case the probe is replaced later.\n- Range -40...+130 °C = approx. 84...150 Ohm. Reference resistor 430 Ohm (standard for Pt100).\n- Input filter / ESD as in the datasheet application circuit.\n- Lead resistance: compensated by a calibration offset in firmware (replaces trimmer 3R1, 10 Ohm).\n- Sensor connector matching the original 4-pole plug from the work space (B1 + B3 - verify V2). B3 goes straight to Specimen_Protection, no electronics.\n- SPI shared with the display; own chip select PT_CS and DRDY to the MCU.\n- Option for later: second MAX31865 for a reference or specimen Pt100.\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- MAX31865AAP+ (SSOP-20, easier to hand solder) or MAX31865ATP+ (TQFN-20).\n- Rref: 430 Ohm 0.1 % 25 ppm/K, 0805 (Vishay TNPW or Susumu RG series).\n- Connector: Phoenix Contact MSTBA 2,5/4-G-5,08 (5.08 mm) - check against the original plug."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 20.32 0)
		(size 152.4 45)
		(margins 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b12429cb-4fcf-45d7-99b2-d3c140c2208b")
	)
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
